{
  "name": "needs-cycle",
  "description": "Chapter 7: Hire 3 workers, advance 20 ticks, and verify living_quarters (fatigue) auto-queue (#928 — fatigue is the sole gauge; hunger and breakNeed were removed)",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000,
          "employeeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "time resume",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "time resume"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:driller",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"driller\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -1000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:hauler",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee hire role:hauler"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Left unmarked: \"hauler\" isn't a real hire role (commandOutput: \"Usage: employee hire role:(driller|blaster|driver|surveyor|manager)\") -- there is no hire button for it, this step is a genuine no-op in both modes.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": 0
        },
        "note": "confirms the fake-role hire is a real no-op, not a silent success"
      },
      "role": "bootstrap",
      "commandOutcome": "refused"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:surveyor",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 2
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -1200
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "build living_quarters at:5,5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"build\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-build-panel [data-build-type=\"living_quarters\"] .bs-build-buy-btn"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 5,
          "z": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Per #526: was `build canteen at:5,5`, a phantom BuildingType (commandOutput: \"Unknown subcommand or building type\") with no catalog row to click -- \"canteen\" maps to the real living_quarters building, which is what the fatigue gauge (#928 — the sole remaining gauge) actually replenishes against (NEED_REST_BUILDING_TYPES, balance.ts). Converted to a real player click on the Build panel, following building-menu-visual.json's pickTile pattern.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "orderedBuildingCount": 1
        },
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -10000
        },
        "note": "Ordering only queues a construction site (#556); the lone driller hired above walks over and builds it during the tick blocks below, so this step asserts the site and the ticks that follow are what make it real."
      },
      "role": "player"
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 40",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 40"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash",
          "minFatigue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "resolveEventIfPending"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Resolved through the event dialog's own buttons. Decides whether an event is pending from authoritative game state, not from whether the modal has rendered -- a DOM-only probe silently missed events on a no-GPU runner where a frame costs ~6s, leaving them pending so later ticks halted and the run diverged while still passing command mode.",
      "role": "player",
      "commandOutcome": "either"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    }
  ]
}
